    "description": "Waterman's\nBlack Dip Pen with Original Presentation Case\nEarly to Mid-20th Century\nThis vintage Waterman's writing instrument features a slender, elongated black tapered staff paired with a decorative gold-tone ferrule and metal nib assembly with an attached reservoir clip. Housed in an authentic hinged Waterman's clamshell presentation case with cream-colored ribbed fabric lining and branded silk-screened satin lid, this piece exemplifies classic early to mid-20th century desk pen design and stationery presentation.\nBlack finished tapered staff holder with knurled gold-tone metal ferrule collar\nFitted metal writing nib featuring an integrated ink reservoir attachment\nAuthentic hinged Waterman's presentation box with tan textured exterior and lined interior\n\"Waterman's\" maker name clearly printed across the interior lid satin liner\nPen length measures approximately 8 inches overall\nCondition:\nVintage condition consistent with age and prior use. Staff shows light surface wear and minor scuffing along the black finish. The metal nib displays significant ink residue, surface oxidation, and finish wear across the reservoir clip. Presentation case hinges properly and latches securely; interior satin exhibits light foxing and ink staining along the edge corners, with exterior showing minor shelf wear.\nTHANK YOU FOR YOUR PURCHASE!\nIf you’re happy and you know it, please leave a 5-star rating! If there is a problem with your order, please contact us via Shop Goodwill before opening returns/claims. We strive to return all messages within one business day.\nPlease click the shipping estimate link in the listing to get the shipping costs directly from FedEx.  There will be no discounts or price changes after an auction has ended.\nOur shipping team works hard to get out all orders as quickly as possible, that being said it may take up to 5 business days after payment for your order to ship out.  Once it ships out you will receive tracking information.\n***IMPORTANT*** If your item was damaged in transit, do not throw away anything, including the box or packing materials until we have authorized you to do so. Photos will be required to file insurance claims.\nOur Business hours: Monday - Friday  8:00 am to 4:00 pm Central\nNew items and unique treasures are added daily, come back soon!",
